  "equipment_type": "Split air conditioner BACnet gateway (1 indoor unit)",
  "applies_to": "Panasonic Etherea and RAC (domestic) split indoor units with a CN-CNT connector.",
  "summary": "One-unit Intesis interface that plugs into the CN-CNT socket of a Panasonic Etherea/RAC indoor unit and serves it as BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP (DIP switch). It exposes 35 objects: on/off, mode, setpoint, fan and both vane directions as _command/_status pairs, room temperature, power consumption, errors, run hours, occupancy logic, a remote lock and Panasonic extras (Powerful, Quiet, 8/10 °C freeze protection, ECONAVI/AutoComfort and the human-activity sensor).",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 246000,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The manual's property tables show Present_Value as R for every object; output objects (AO/BO/MO) have a priority array and are shown here as commandable. The occupancy setpoint AVs are shown read-only as printed.",
    "The manual prints the units of the four occupancy setpoint AVs as Hours (71); they are temperatures and are shown here in °C.",
    "There is no RoomTemperature_command object; AI 1 RoomTemperature is the unit's own sensor.",
    "LockRemoteControl (BV 2) state texts are printed as 0=Locked, 1=Unlocked.",
    "Setpoint range is 16-30 °C, or 8-10 °C when freeze protection is on. Temperature objects follow the °C/°F DIP switch.",
    "Different product from the IN485PAN001I000 (MS/TP only), which is listed separately."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Intesis BACnet - Domestic Panasonic AC User Manual (INBACPAN001I000)",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "11/2024 v1.5",
